1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
KURCHI PROJECTS — SHOWROOM WORKFLOW
What is happening: One rollout is managed from first client setup through signed handover.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
STEP 1 — CREATE CLIENT
Admin is adding the client, GST details, contacts and showroom rollout programme.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
STEP 2 — CREATE SHOWROOM PROJECT
Admin is adding the city, site address, opening date and installation team.

4
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
STEP 3 — BUILD THE BOQ
Admin is adding chairs, sofas, storage and tables with quantities, pricing and sourcing.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
STEP 4 — CLIENT APPROVAL
Client is reviewing the agreed scope and approving the BOQ before work begins.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
STEP 5 — PLAN SUPPLIERS
Admin is creating the schedule and issuing purchase orders with promised delivery dates.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
STEP 6 — DISPATCH AND IN TRANSIT
Kurchi is recording crates, transporter, LR, vehicle, challan, e-way bill and ETA.

8
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
STEP 7 — INSTALLATION AT SITE
The installation team receives crates, uploads proof, marks items installed and reports issues.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000
STEP 8 — RESOLVE AND BILL
Admin resolves snags while Accounts creates invoices, records receipts and tracks vendor bills.

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000
STEP 9 — HANDOVER COMPLETE
Client signs handover. The showroom is complete and moves into DLP and retention tracking.
